3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c27f685091c9afca0160c1b990b7061ef56f0d6e5af100d92784362d3845ffe5","event_uuid":"1f063c4e-abb2-449c-b6bb-3a39fe6a9d0f","position":{"commit_sha":"3b03de35d1a3c9158d7e15681a646e322b1120ea","position":"1788262792801204511-1f063c4e-abb2-449c-b6bb-3a39fe6a9d0f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Planning update before claim: added tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py to file_impact because registering a new core command updates the core-command census/count. No code edits have begun; plan-review job 1788257207253240893-d13f689a0fca45c8b0eeeebf9c782401 is running and may need a fresh rerun if it observed the previous file-impact material.","timestamp":1788257376928005417},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation update: offline shadow-clone reclaim-collapse engine is implemented in the s1-collapse-engine worktree. Added RED-first tests for collapse/reduced-state preservation, ledger position re-resolution, enforce_since re-anchor verified by verify-authorship, horizon-ref eligibility enforcement, shadow-clone safety refusal, and CLI dry-run. Targeted suite is green (177 passed), make lint green, make typecheck green. Full non-integration make test was attempted but stopped after an existing lifecycle failure in test_atomic_completion_close.py unrelated to this change; targeted coverage for this story is green.","timestamp":1788260548422183998}],"created_at":1788046507179013893,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"013c79ba-ffc0-46d0-aa61-1727a738a133","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"e32d-6ea1-029a-435d"},{"link_uuid":"88547d1a-be44-4df6-9294-570b58fd6b0d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"866f-440c-3686-42df"},{"link_uuid":"6fa533f5-6527-403c-9b4a-554d569977c1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"9b58a744-4c8b-48d3-9ee9-c94badfbfdee","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d075-03c2-afee-46a0"},{"link_uuid":"8935b66b-8097-49fd-940e-a5d9008e0297","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"45f8-869e-0112-4abb"}],"description":"## Context\n\nParent epic `polite-antivirus-bedbug` proves the ONLY lever that shrinks the blobless CI-guarded `tickets` pack is reducing reachable commit+tree objects via **below-horizon history collapse**. This story builds the offline rewrite ENGINE (tooling + tests + a dry-run), stopping before any prod mutation.\n\n## Scope\n\nImplement, as an offline operation over a disposable shadow clone, the collapse of below-horizon derived commits/trees (enrichment-quartet duplicates, superseded `TICKET_DIGEST`s, redundant auto-reconcile merges, and the re-emitted root/ticket trees) into SNAPSHOT-anchored checkpoints, using core-git `git fast-import` (NOT third-party `git filter-repo` — not vendored; portability). Reconcile the authorship ledger: re-resolve each `position` (`{ts}-{uuid}`, invariant across the rewrite) to its NEW `commit_sha` and re-anchor `identity.enforce_since` to the new baseline so `verify_authorship_at_commit`'s ancestry era-check evaluates consistently. Eligibility comes from `able-tidy-massasauga`; the horizon/boundary from `unlikely-zealous-skua` / ADR 0106.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n1. Add `rebar._commands.reclaim_collapse`, an offline engine and CLI handler that accepts an explicit shadow clone root plus optional source/ref/dry-run arguments. It will refuse to run unless the target is explicitly marked as a shadow clone, is not the configured live tracker path, and has no push-capable remotes, so S1 cannot mutate prod.\n2. Build a reduced-state preflight from the target ticket worktree, choose a boundary commit through the landed `reclaim_eligibility.checkpoint_commit_eligible` predicate plus ADR 0106 folded/below-horizon rules, then construct a fast-import stream. The stream emits a parentless checkpoint with the boundary tree and replays retained commits above the boundary with preserved author/committer/message/timestamps and rewritten parent marks.\n3. After importing, reconcile retained SNAPSHOT payloads before finalizing the rewritten branch: use `authorship_resolution.build_position_commit_map` against the rewritten graph to replace every ledger `position.commit_sha` with the new commit for that invariant `position`. Emit the updated tree through fast-import so C5 has no dangling preimage commit references.\n4. Re-anchor the returned offline config guidance to the rewritten baseline: the result reports the checkpoint SHA as the required `identity.enforce_since` value for verification against the shadow branch. The engine does not edit repo config by default; tests may pass the value through `REBAR_IDENTITY_ENFORCE_SINCE` to prove `verify-authorship` is clean.\n5. Register `reclaim-collapse` in the lazy CLI registry with a parser under `_cli/_parsers/core/reclaim.py`; regenerate committed CLI help/reference artifacts.\n\n## Test plan\n\nRED-first tests in `tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py` create synthetic disposable git ticket stores, not the live tracker. They cover: (a) collapse to a parentless checkpoint through `git fast-import`; (b) reducer-state equality before vs. after in reduced form; (c) position-to-new-commit ledger re-resolution; (d) `identity.enforce_since` re-anchor reported/usable by `verify-authorship`; and (e) refusal for non-shadow/prod-like targets and push-capable remotes. The happy-path collapse test stays visible to the implementer; edge/E2E safety/authorship tests are held out and restored for validation.\n\n## Surface-parity census\n\n- CLI command: in scope, proven through `rebar reclaim-collapse` parser/handler tests.\n- MCP/API tool: out of scope; S1 is an offline local-code operation, not a tracker mutation surface. S2 may add publish/swap APIs.\n- Library facade: out of scope for public `import rebar`; this story introduces an internal command module only.\n- Automated callers: out of scope; no scheduler or prod publish is added in S1.\n- Dual-direction mirror: out of scope; this is an offline rewrite/dry-run only and has no inbound/outbound mirror operation.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nPublishing/swapping the rewritten history to any remote (that is S2), any prod mutation, feature-branch/publish locks, S3 auto-doctor bypass, and any third-party rewrite dependency.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The engine collapses below-horizon derived commits/trees to SNAPSHOT checkpoints on a shadow clone via core-git `git fast-import` (no third-party rewrite tool).\n- [ ] The authorship ledger is reconciled: every `position` re-resolves to its new `commit_sha` and `enforce_since` is re-anchored to the new baseline.\n- [ ] `rebar verify-authorship` is clean on the rewritten shadow branch (no unverifiable mutating event).\n- [ ] Above-horizon history and all still-observable ticket state are bit-identical in reduced form before vs after (a reducer-state equality fixture passes).\n- [ ] Unit/integration tests cover the collapse, the ledger re-resolution, and the enforce_since re-anchor.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No prod `tickets` remote is mutated by this story (offline shadow clone only).\n\n## Portability\n\nThe rewrite primitive is core-git (`git fast-import` plus ordinary tree construction), present wherever git is; no dependence on any single CI provider or third-party history rewrite tool.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_collapse.py","reason":"New offline shadow-clone collapse engine and CLI handler; uses core git fast-import, refuses non-shadow targets, rewrites tickets ref only in the disposable clone, reconciles SNAPSHOT authorship ledgers and emits config overrides for identity.enforce_since re-anchor."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reclaim.py","reason":"Argparse parser factory for the new reclaim-collapse dry-run command."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"Register the reclaim-collapse route with lazy parser/handler metadata."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/reclaim-collapse.txt","reason":"Generated runtime help for the new command."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"Generated CLI overview must include the new visible command."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Generated CLI reference must include the new command."},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"Document the public reclaim-collapse dispatcher arm's exit-code contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reclaim_collapse.py","reason":"RED-first unit/integration coverage for the collapse, reducer-state equality, ledger position->commit_sha re-resolution, enforce_since re-anchor, verify-authorship clean, fast-import use, and shadow-only safeguards."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_core_cli_parsers.py","reason":"Core command inventory count/census must include the new registered core command."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","866f-440c-3686-42df"],["depends_on","e32d-6ea1-029a-435d"],["parent","536b-8930-b922-4063"],["relates_to","45f8-869e-0112-4abb"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","d075-03c2-afee-46a0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","parent_status_uuid":"b8d23d50-293c-4065-b960-4a5466e0597e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bdf3-e7e3-c96f-4b9f","ticket_type":"story","title":"S1: below-horizon commit/tree collapse rewrite engine (offline, shadow clone)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f9ef7e7a-7213-494a-847c-2e5f3efe184a","ebe5a891-0ed5-4ed8-9265-b2cb5f4254b3","6fa533f5-6527-403c-9b4a-554d569977c1","f6285f3a-4b08-479f-af05-ed7b34867003","078538b3-4d90-4451-aff9-cb8b5fb52bf1","7e6d02ee-092d-41f0-b18d-8f9f23483f47","b8d23d50-293c-4065-b960-4a5466e0597e","472b390f-8de6-46c1-987b-1278608eaded","9b58a744-4c8b-48d3-9ee9-c94badfbfdee","aa206c59-20a6-4c6d-b82c-355e600d3dfa","8935b66b-8097-49fd-940e-a5d9008e0297","1f063c4e-abb2-449c-b6bb-3a39fe6a9d0f"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788262792801204512,"uuid":"1f5536ae-ee8e-4b44-b1d0-8eb62fd543b6"}